      "item_body": "<p>[K/U] For each function, determine the critical points and whether it is a local maximum point or a local minimum point, or neither. Is the tangent to the graph at each point parallel to the horizontal axis?</p>\n<p>a. h(x) = -6x^3 + 18x^2 + 3; critical points: <span id=\"blank_cff0541b-bb6f-446d-9f0a-e95a6af54d54\"></span> (<span id=\"blank_1fd12a19-4e06-48c8-a971-f51436a85793\"></span>), tangent <span id=\"blank_89a1c962-e7ad-4216-a869-549a7b7931d3\"></span>; <span id=\"blank_a3851c2e-4261-4162-9bf3-4747ce849f8e\"></span> (<span id=\"blank_d02e6ce9-0d92-4141-8b87-b02d0e8aec33\"></span>), tangent <span id=\"blank_ba245554-b87d-412c-9930-0fb59d011881\"></span></p>\n<p>b. g(t) = t^5 + t^3; critical point: <span id=\"blank_26cc4d99-9592-4f17-914c-350f6fc6a726\"></span> (<span id=\"blank_60dbc14b-38d1-4d18-a0cf-3ede8aea8dee\"></span>), tangent <span id=\"blank_b351a011-4f7f-4f3b-b587-dfedd7ff28b0\"></span></p>\n<p>c. y = (x - 5)^(1/3); critical point: <span id=\"blank_05c1964e-ed4f-4dfa-87ab-d83deabeae0a\"></span> (<span id=\"blank_7c1219fd-cd4d-42d5-8a69-801ed3b5553e\"></span>), tangent <span id=\"blank_a0ef3a5d-6fc9-409f-ad72-36e9a1e6e57c\"></span></p>\n<p>d. f(x) = (x^2 - 1)^(1/3); critical points: <span id=\"blank_3766e4b9-9ffd-4ec6-9835-7e02fdf2a424\"></span> (<span id=\"blank_168d3e68-e2d9-42d4-b4f6-316ade77f1c2\"></span>), tangent <span id=\"blank_625ffed2-349f-40b3-afa3-03115463e793\"></span>; <span id=\"blank_4efe077f-6ef7-4746-891e-3468774bb7f0\"></span> (<span id=\"blank_e3e80ab0-2751-4174-91d8-19f6fc47cfb9\"></span>), tangent <span id=\"blank_56ae5777-f6f5-4958-84de-5762eccb6fcb\"></span>; <span id=\"blank_1bf8b384-786c-44f2-82a8-ffef45e5a575\"></span> (<span id=\"blank_1e339947-3a6f-4941-994c-67e4993ce943\"></span>), tangent <span id=\"blank_1b88b4cf-b317-487a-b223-d6c1f7dc5c5b\"></span></p>",
